n.json", "diagnostics": {"kind": "agriculture", "training_end": 2018, "n": 60, "rmse": 0.06000061973006384, "crps": 0.029388616378595325, "coverage90": 0.9333333333333333, "type": "Bayesian conditional holdout with realized inputs; latest revised history"}, "evidence_ids": ["7bec50c5aa2cba9f3fcba42c"]}, {"artifact": "reports/fiscal_bayesian_validation.json", "diagnostics": {"kind": "fiscal", "training_end": 2018, "n": 66, "rmse": 0.08244289244070911, "crps": 0.04571586072955261, "coverage90": 0.9393939393939394, "type": "Bayesian conditional holdout with realized inputs; latest revised history"}, "evidence_ids": ["48658736654193b4b92b3460"]}, {"artifact": "reports/macro_validation.csv", "diagnostics": [{"kind": "agriculture", "model": "baseline", "n": 180, "rmse": 0.056136846029297, "crps": 0.028122554109536, "coverage90": 0.872222222222222, "validation_type": "conditional final-vintage rolling hindcast; ridge challenger"}, {"kind": "agriculture", "model": "with_climate", "n": 180, "rmse": 0.05875595099814, "crps": 0.031469330927203, "coverage90": 0.738888888888889, "validation_type": "conditional final-vintage rolling hindcast; ridge challenger"}, {"kind": "fiscal", "model": "baseline", "n": 180, "rmse": 0.09057917685843, "crps": 0.048746893623015, "coverage90": 0.827777777777778, "validation_type": "conditional final-vintage rolling hindcast; ridge challenger"}, {"kind": "fiscal", "model": "with_agriculture", "n": 180, "rmse": 0.093557833187244, "crps": 0.050640051295598, "coverage90": 0.811111111111111, "validation_type": "conditional final-vintage rolling hindcast; ridge challenger"}], "evidence_ids": ["fcd942bceffdc9776e5c28fd"], "limitation": "Conditional final-vintage ridge challenger comparisons; not direct validation of Bayesian posterior forecasts."}]}}
{"time": 1790986626.1499784, "type": "model_turn", "turn": 2, "response": {"calls": [{"id": "call_-7231415682993219303", "name": "submit_findings", "arguments": {"claims": [{"evidence_ids": ["7abd5499be5a9a5a842fb1da"], "kind": "descriptive", "text": "Sampler diagnostics (R-hat, effective sample size, divergences, and other posterior checks) only establish that the posterior draws were computed reliably; they say nothing about whether the fitted model makes useful predictions beyond its training data."}, {"evidence_ids": ["7bec50c5aa2cba9f3fcba42c", "48658736654193b4b92b3460"], "kind": "interpretation", "text": "The strongest available out-of-sample evidence here is Bayesian conditional holdout validation, in which models trained through an earlier cutoff were scored on held-out outcomes using realized inputs. Predictive accuracy, sharpness, and interval coverage measures from such holdouts, not diagnostics, are the basis for any out-of-sample claim."}, {"evidence_ids": ["fcd942bceffdc9776e5c28fd"], "kind": "interpretation", "text": "Rolling hindcasts on final-vintage data provide complementary evidence, but these were run with a ridge challenger rather than the Bayesian posterior itself, so they cannot directly validate the posterior forecasts actually used for the risk estimates."}, {"evidence_ids": ["7bec50c5aa2cba9f3fcba42c", "48658736654193b4b92b3460"], "kind": "interpretation", "text": "Even the holdout exercises are conditional: they feed realized, latest-revised inputs to the models. To claim useful out-of-sample forecasts for the assessment's forward-looking risk numbers, one would additionally need validation under genuinely forecast-time inputs, since the published risk figures condition on climate outlook vintages and external growth projections rather than realized values."}, {"evidence_ids": ["7abd5499be5a9a5a842fb1da", "fcd942bceffdc9776e5c28fd"], "kind": "interpretation", "text": "Additional evidence needed beyond convergence diagnostics includes: prospective forecast verification against outcomes realized after the assessment; calibration of tail measures such as value-at-risk and expected shortfall, not just central predictive accuracy; comparisons against a null or naive benchmark to show the model beats a simple alternative; robustness to data vintage, since results are fitted on revised rather than real-time data; and demonstration that skill holds for the specific event and period being forecast rather than only in-sample or near-sample conditions."}, {"evidence_ids": ["7abd5499be5a9a5a842fb1da"], "kind": "interpretation", "text": "In short, useful out-of-sample forecasting is an empirical property of predictions compared with realized outcomes and suitable benchmarks; converged samplers are a necessary computational check but never sufficient evidence of predictive skill."}], "limitations": ["Sampler diagnostics for both model components pass, but convergence cannot demonstrate predictive skill.", "Holdout and hindcast validation is conditional on realized, latest-revised inputs and does not validate forecasts made under real-time climate outlook vintages.", "Rolling hindcasts were computed with a ridge challenger, not the Bayesian posterior used for the published risk estimates.", "No prospective verification against outcomes occurring after the assessment date is available.", "The models are conditional ENSO-response models without causal identification, so accuracy claims are conditional on the stated ENSO scenario and input assumptions."], "title": "Evidence needed for out-of-sample forecast claims"}}], "text": "", "reasoning_content": "The question: what evidence beyond diagnostics needed to claim useful out-of-sample forecasts. Answer with findings citing diagnostics artifacts. Submit findings: descriptive/interpretation claims, no digits in prose. Evidence IDs available.", "input_tokens": 16966, "output_tokens": 804}, "cost_usd": 0.02729}
